 "An old plant-derived medicine for gout attacks. Low doses work as well as high doses, with far fewer side effects. Overdose is dangerous.",
 "Colchicine eases gout attacks if started early, and prevents flares when starting urate-lowering treatment. The modern low-dose regimen is as effective as the old ‘until diarrhoea’ approach. It has a narrow safety margin and serious interactions.",
