 "A twice-yearly injection that strongly protects bones, but its effect wears off fast. Never just stop it: you need a plan.",
 "Denosumab blocks a signal that switches on bone-resorbing cells. It reduces spine fractures by about two-thirds. Unlike bisphosphonates, it doesn’t stay in bone: if a dose is late or stopped, bone loss rebounds and multiple spine fractures can happen, so a bisphosphonate is usually given afterwards.",
